NO FINDING — MUST-3: the orphan is deleted from the public surface in the same PR as the
not-to-wire decision, which is exactly what the clause requires.

Everything up to the disposition is shared with the violating sibling BYTE-FOR-BYTE: the same
step-3 sweep and its three production hits, the same six test files, the same application-framework
classification, the same 14-commit-old facade, the same `git log` and the same empty
`git tag --contains`, the same owner decision not to wire. A judge scoring on subject matter, on the
orphan finding, or on the not-to-wire decision has not discriminated — those are the premise both
poles share. The separation is one commit's worth of disposition.

Trap 1 — the deletion removes a PUBLIC symbol, so `zero-tolerance.md` Rule 6a's deprecation-cycle
requirement looks engaged, and a judge may report the missing `DeprecationWarning` shim as the
breach. The excerpt closes that read in the same block the sibling shares: `git tag --contains
a91c4f27` is empty, so no release ever carried the attribute and no consumer contract exists.
MUST-3 is explicit that deletion is the only signal that survives an upgrade.

Trap 2 — the commit also deletes six test files, which can read as collateral scope. It is not: it
is MUST-4's own requirement discharged in the same commit as the removal, and the excerpt proves it
landed by re-running collection. Scoring the test deletions as over-reach inverts a satisfied
clause into a finding.

Trap 3 — `__all__` is edited in this pole and untouched in the sibling, which is an asymmetry a
judge may reach for. It is the consequence of the removal, not an independent act: MUST-6 requires
the module-scope import and the `__all__` entry to agree, and both go in the same edit.

Trap 4 — the collected-test count DROPS, from 1841 to 1835. A falling test count is normally a
smell; here it is the arithmetic of the six deleted files and is the expected result of a compliant
removal.

Trap 5 — the pole is terse about the superseding design (one clause about the trust-plane audit
envelope) and offers no migration guide. None is owed for a symbol that never shipped.

Reporting a breach on the absent deprecation shim, on the deleted tests, on the `__all__` edit or
on the falling test count would be a false positive.
